  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1238 AM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nTemperatures will continue to increase as we head into the middle of \nthe week, with NBM spitting out a number off 100+ degree \ntemperatures for Wednesday afternoon. Factor in our dew points and \nWednesday is looking like it could be a day for some heat headlines \nfor at least portions of the area. That being said, I think we will \nstill be somewhat borderline, and the issuance could go either way \ndepending on how things trend. Regardless, Wednesday and Thursday \nwill be hot across the region and precaution should be used if you \nare spending an extended period of time outdoors. \n\nThe last half of the week becomes a little more tricky to forecast. \nWhile it will still be hot, we are keeping an eye on the tropics as \nTropical Depression 2 formed in the northeastern Gulf. This system \nwill slowly move westward through the northern Gulf through late \nTuesday or Wednesday before moving towards the upper or middle Texas \ncoast Thursday into Friday. There is much uncertainty with the track \nand intensity of this system and the impact that it will have on our \nregion. Being that we are not far removed from recent flooding \nacross the area, we will continue to monitor this situation closely. \nIt is important to make sure that you use trusted sources throughout \nthe week to find out the latest information.",
